window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-009.json",{"day":9,"title":"What a Health Notice Can and Cannot Do","targetWords":[{"word":"sick","gloss":"生病的","context":"It described the clinic’s assessment process and encouraged people who felt sick to seek suitable professional advice.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"emergency","gloss":"紧急情况","context":"A pregnant worker asked where she should go in an emergency.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"blind","gloss":"失明的","context":"A blind resident pointed out that a printed warning excluded him altogether.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"disorder","gloss":"疾病","context":"A chronic disorder such as diabetes required continued care even during the outbreak.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"fatal","gloss":"致命的","context":"Early drafts emphasized a deadly virus and a fatal outcome, alarming readers without explaining what help was available.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"chronic","gloss":"慢性的","context":"A chronic disorder such as diabetes required continued care even during the outbreak.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"hazard","gloss":"危险","context":"A separate section addressed the hazard of misinformation.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"immune","gloss":"有免疫力的","context":"Toxic substances advertised as a cure could poison users, while untreated water might infect a person who believed he was immune.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"fatigue","gloss":"疲劳","context":"A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"surgery","gloss":"外科手术","context":"Surgery, therapy, and a transplant were not interchangeable promises of recovery.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"epidemic","gloss":"传染病流行","context":"When a regional epidemic reached the town, the public clinic needed a notice that people would actually understand.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"addict","gloss":"成瘾者","context":"An addict seeking help for cocaine or heroin deserved confidentiality rather than public blame.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"therapy","gloss":"治疗","context":"Surgery, therapy, and a transplant were not interchangeable promises of recovery.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"virus","gloss":"病毒","context":"Early drafts emphasized a deadly virus and a fatal outcome, alarming readers without explaining what help was available.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"wound","gloss":"伤口","context":"A wound could damage tissue, and an acute problem might require urgent assessment, but none of these facts justified improvising instructions in a general public notice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"asleep","gloss":"睡着","context":"Someone might remain awake because of worry, while another fell asleep from exhaustion.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"headache","gloss":"头痛","context":"A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"clinic","gloss":"诊所","context":"When a regional epidemic reached the town, the public clinic needed a notice that people would actually understand.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dose","gloss":"剂量","context":"A vaccine and a pill served different purposes; a dose could not be chosen simply because a neighbor recommended it.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"toxic","gloss":"有毒的","context":"Toxic substances advertised as a cure could poison users, while untreated water might infect a person who believed he was immune.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"syndrome","gloss":"综合症","context":"A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"deadly","gloss":"致命的","context":"Early drafts emphasized a deadly virus and a fatal outcome, alarming readers without explaining what help was available.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"diagnose","gloss":"诊断","context":"The notice therefore avoided trying to diagnose readers from a list.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"awake","gloss":"醒着的","context":"Someone might remain awake because of worry, while another fell asleep from exhaustion.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"infect","gloss":"感染","context":"Toxic substances advertised as a cure could poison users, while untreated water might infect a person who believed he was immune.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"tissue","gloss":"组织","context":"A wound could damage tissue, and an acute problem might require urgent assessment, but none of these facts justified improvising instructions in a general public notice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"acute","gloss":"急性的","context":"A wound could damage tissue, and an acute problem might require urgent assessment, but none of these facts justified improvising instructions in a general public notice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"diabetes","gloss":"糖尿病","context":"A chronic disorder such as diabetes required continued care even during the outbreak.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"poison","gloss":"使中毒","context":"Toxic substances advertised as a cure could poison users, while untreated water might infect a person who believed he was immune.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"vaccine","gloss":"疫苗","context":"A vaccine and a pill served different purposes; a dose could not be chosen simply because a neighbor recommended it.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"fever","gloss":"发烧","context":"A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pill","gloss":"药丸","context":"A vaccine and a pill served different purposes; a dose could not be chosen simply because a neighbor recommended it.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"breakdown","gloss":"瓦解","context":"Historic references to plague showed how rumor could produce a social breakdown alongside disease.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"inject","gloss":"注射","context":"Even when staff needed to inject a medicine, they explained the reason instead of assuming consent.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"ache","gloss":"疼痛","context":"A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"cough","gloss":"咳嗽","context":"A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"transplant","gloss":"移植","context":"Surgery, therapy, and a transplant were not interchangeable promises of recovery.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"sweat","gloss":"汗","context":"A nurse might ask whether a patient tended to bleed easily or had noticed unusual sweat, but such questions belonged in a private consultation.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"bleed","gloss":"出血","context":"A nurse might ask whether a patient tended to bleed easily or had noticed unusual sweat, but such questions belonged in a private consultation.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"cocaine","gloss":"可卡因","context":"An addict seeking help for cocaine or heroin deserved confidentiality rather than public blame.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"plague","gloss":"瘟疫","context":"Historic references to plague showed how rumor could produce a social breakdown alongside disease.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"casualty","gloss":"伤者","context":"A dental appointment, a fracture assessment, and support for a casualty of an accident should not disappear from view.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"dental","gloss":"牙科的","context":"A dental appointment, a fracture assessment, and support for a casualty of an accident should not disappear from view.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"pregnant","gloss":"怀孕的","context":"A pregnant worker asked where she should go in an emergency.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"chill","gloss":"寒战","context":"A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"heroin","gloss":"海洛因","context":"An addict seeking help for cocaine or heroin deserved confidentiality rather than public blame.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"invalid","gloss":"病弱者（旧称）","context":"Old terms such as “invalid” and “cripple” reduced people to conditions; the revised notice instead described the support a resident needed and the services that could provide it.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"cripple","gloss":"残疾者（旧称）","context":"Old terms such as “invalid” and “cripple” reduced people to conditions; the revised notice instead described the support a resident needed and the services that could provide it.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"fracture","gloss":"骨折","context":"A dental appointment, a fracture assessment, and support for a casualty of an accident should not disappear from view.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"hygiene","gloss":"卫生","context":"Good hygiene remained part of a broader system, not a substitute for access to treatment.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"When a regional epidemic reached the town, the public clinic needed a notice that people would actually understand. Early drafts emphasized a deadly virus and a fatal outcome, alarming readers without explaining what help was available. A blind resident pointed out that a printed warning excluded him altogether. A pregnant worker asked where she should go in an emergency. The communications team realized that a useful message had to connect fear with practical access, rather than make danger sound inevitable.","zh":"地区性传染病流行波及城镇时，公共诊所需要一份居民真正看得懂的通知。最初草稿强调致命病毒与死亡结局，让人恐慌，却没解释哪里可以获得帮助。一位盲人指出，单靠纸质警告把他完全排除在外。一位怀孕的工人询问紧急情况下该去哪里。传播团队意识到，有用的信息应把担忧与求助途径联系起来，而不是让危险显得无法避免。"},{"en":"Doctors helped distinguish different experiences of illness. A cough, fever, chill, headache, or ache could have more than one cause, and fatigue alone could not identify a particular syndrome. Someone might remain awake because of worry, while another fell asleep from exhaustion. A chronic disorder such as diabetes required continued care even during the outbreak. The notice therefore avoided trying to diagnose readers from a list. It described the clinic’s assessment process and encouraged people who felt sick to seek suitable professional advice.","zh":"医生帮助区分不同的患病体验。咳嗽、发热、寒战、头痛或其他疼痛可能有多种原因，仅凭疲劳无法识别某种特定综合征。有人因担忧而失眠，也有人因疲惫入睡。糖尿病之类的慢性疾病，即使在疫情期间仍需要持续照护。因此，通知避免用一张清单替读者诊断，而是介绍诊所的评估流程，并鼓励不舒服的人寻求适当的专业建议。"},{"en":"The writers also reviewed familiar misunderstandings about treatment. A vaccine and a pill served different purposes; a dose could not be chosen simply because a neighbor recommended it. Surgery, therapy, and a transplant were not interchangeable promises of recovery. Even when staff needed to inject a medicine, they explained the reason instead of assuming consent. A wound could damage tissue, and an acute problem might require urgent assessment, but none of these facts justified improvising instructions in a general public notice.","zh":"写作者也检查了对治疗的常见误解。疫苗与药片用途不同，剂量不能仅根据邻居的推荐决定。手术、治疗和移植也不是可以随意互换的康复承诺。即使医护人员需要注射药物，也会解释原因，而不是默认患者同意。伤口可能损伤组织，急性问题可能需要紧急评估，但这些事实都不意味着可以在面向公众的普通通知里擅自编写操作指导。"},{"en":"A separate section addressed the hazard of misinformation. Toxic substances advertised as a cure could poison users, while untreated water might infect a person who believed he was immune. Historic references to plague showed how rumor could produce a social breakdown alongside disease. An addict seeking help for cocaine or heroin deserved confidentiality rather than public blame. Old terms such as “invalid” and “cripple” reduced people to conditions; the revised notice instead described the support a resident needed and the services that could provide it.","zh":"另一部分讨论错误信息的危险。被宣传为疗法的有毒物质可能使使用者中毒；未经处理的水也可能让自以为免疫的人感染。历史上的瘟疫案例表明，谣言会在疾病之外引发社会秩序的瓦解。因可卡因或海洛因成瘾而求助的人，应获得隐私保护，而非公开指责。旧式称呼把人缩减为“病弱者”或“残疾者”；修订后的通知转而说明居民需要何种支持，以及哪些服务能够提供支持。"},{"en":"Finally, the clinic linked outbreak planning with ordinary care. A dental appointment, a fracture assessment, and support for a casualty of an accident should not disappear from view. A nurse might ask whether a patient tended to bleed easily or had noticed unusual sweat, but such questions belonged in a private consultation. Good hygiene remained part of a broader system, not a substitute for access to treatment. The final notice was less dramatic than the first draft, and considerably more useful. Readers helped test whether key information could be found quickly, and the clinic provided the same explanation in accessible formats, recognizing that clarity also depended on how a message was delivered. Staff also explained where readers could ask for clarification without having to disclose private information in public.","zh":"最后，诊所把疫情规划与日常照护联系起来。牙科预约、骨折评估和事故伤者的救助，不应被完全忽视。护士可能询问病人是否容易出血，或是否出现异常出汗，但这些问题应在私人诊疗中讨论。良好卫生习惯是整体体系的一部分，不能取代治疗的可及性。最终通知没有初稿那样耸人听闻，却有用得多。读者帮助检验关键信息能否迅速找到，诊所还通过无障碍形式提供相同解释，因为清晰与否也取决于信息如何传递。员工还说明读者可以在哪里请求解释，而不必公开私人信息。"}],"previous":8,"next":10});
